at line 100, with no change needed in the command file.

## 4. Parity suite skip

### 4.1 New file: `tests/parity/conftest.py`

Reads `shared/global-config-rules.json` relative to the repository root and
exposes a module-level helper that raises `pytest.skip` with
`allow_module_level=True` when `python` is present in `disabled_runtimes`. The
skip reason must name the disabled runtime and state that the suite re-enables
automatically when the list is emptied.

Visible skips are required rather than `collect_ignore`, so the deferral is
reported on every run instead of disappearing silently.

### 4.2 Modified: the four parity modules

Add the module-level guard call immediately after the imports in each of
`tests/parity/test_cli_parity.py`, `tests/parity/test_global_config_parity.py`,
`tests/parity/test_jenkins_parity.py`, and `tests/parity/test_setup_parity.py`.

No test bodies, assertions, or the 127 Python launcher call sites are modified
or deleted.

### 4.3 Not modified

`tests/unit/` is left entirely alone. Those tests import the frozen Python
package directly and continue to pass; they are not parity tests and are not
gated.

